UxPlay: play an ordinary http(s) AirPlay video address directly.

UxPlay 1.73.7 plays AirPlay video only in the form the YouTube app sends,
an address ending in /master.m3u8 that it fetches through the phone, and
answered anything else with 400 "Could not find valid Plist Data". Plex,
and other apps that AirPlay an ordinary stream, send an address the
television can fetch itself (Plex: an HLS playlist on the Plex server).
This hands such an address straight to UxPlay's own video player, from
the position the phone gave, instead of refusing it.

Checked on a real television: an episode AirPlayed from Plex on an iPad
buffered, then played from where the iPad was, with its position and
length reported back to the iPad.

--- a/lib/http_handlers.h
+++ b/lib/http_handlers.h
@@ -889,6 +889,23 @@
 
     /* we only support HLS if the playback location is terminated by "/master.m3u8" */
     const char *uri_suffix = strstr(playback_location, "/master.m3u8");
+    if (!uri_suffix && (!strncmp(playback_location, "http://", 7) ||
+                        !strncmp(playback_location, "https://", 8))) {
+        /* FreeTVOS: an address the television can fetch for itself. Plex, and
+           other apps that AirPlay an ordinary http(s) stream, send one; the
+           YouTube form above is fetched through the client instead. Play it
+           directly from where the client was, rather than refusing it. */
+        logger_log(raop->logger, LOGGER_INFO, "playing Content-Location directly (%s)",
+                   strncmp(playback_location, "https://", 8) ? "http" : "https");
+        set_playback_location(airplay_video, playback_location, strlen(playback_location));
+        raop->callbacks.on_video_play(raop->callbacks.cls, playback_location,
+                                      start_position_seconds);
+        plist_mem_free(playback_location);
+        if (req_root_node) {
+            plist_free(req_root_node);
+        }
+        return;
+    }
     if (!uri_suffix) { 
         logger_log(raop->logger, LOGGER_ERR, "Content-Location has unsupported form:\n%s\n", playback_location);	    
         goto play_error;
